page({file:'privacy.html',title:`Privacy | ${NAME}`,desc:`What ${NAME} collects (your email if you subscribe, anonymous cookieless page events), who processes it (Kit, Stripe via Kit, Cloudflare) and how to get it deleted.`,body:`${legalHero('Privacy','Privacy, in plain words.',`${NAME} is a free AI API price ledger at ratecardai.pages.dev. We collect as little as we can: your email only if you give it to us, and anonymous page events with no cookies.`)}
${prose(`<h2 class="h3">What we collect and why</h2><ul>
<li><b>Email newsletter.</b> If you subscribe, your email address goes to <a href="https://kit.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Kit</a> (ConvertKit), our email provider, with double opt-in. Kit stores it and standard email data (opens, clicks) so we can send the weekly digest. Every email has a one-click unsubscribe. Legal basis: your consent.</li>
<li><b>Purchases (Pro, sponsor slot).</b> Checkout runs on Kit’s hosted pages (o11y-watch.kit.com); card payments are processed by Kit’s payment processor, Stripe. We never see or store your card number. We receive the order record (name, email, product, amount) from Kit. Legal basis: performing the contract, plus tax and accounting duties.</li>
<li><b>Anonymous usage events, no cookies.</b> A small first-party script (<a href="/assets/grow.js">/assets/grow.js</a>) sends events such as page view, clicks on checkout or signup buttons and form submits to our own Cloudflare Worker, which stores them in Cloudflare Workers Analytics Engine. Each event holds the site, page path, button label, UTM campaign tags, referring domain and an A/B test label. It does <b>not</b> include your IP address, the email you type, or any cookie or user ID. Legal basis: legitimate interest in knowing which pages help people.</li>
<li><b>On your device.</b> We use your browser’s local storage (not cookies) for UTM tags for up to 7 days (<code>grow:utm</code>) and A/B test assignment (<code>grow:ab:*</code>). A service worker caches pages so the site works offline. Clearing site data removes all of it.</li>
<li><b>Hosting.</b> The site is served by Cloudflare Pages. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes your IP address to deliver pages and block abuse, under <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare’s privacy policy</a>.</li></ul>
<h2 class="h3">What we don’t do</h2><ul><li>No advertising trackers, no third-party analytics cookies, no selling or renting your data.</li><li>Sponsors never receive subscriber emails.</li></ul>
<h2 class="h3">How long we keep it</h2><ul><li>Email: until you unsubscribe or ask us to delete it.</li><li>Order records: as long as tax and accounting rules require.</li><li>Anonymous events: as long as Cloudflare Analytics Engine retains them (about three months).</li></ul>
<h2 class="h3">Your rights and deleting your data</h2><p>You can unsubscribe from any email in one click. To see, correct or delete what we hold about you, email <a href="${CONTACT}">${MAIL}</a> from the address concerned with the subject “Delete my data” (or “Access my data”). We remove you from Kit and delete what we are not legally required to keep, and confirm by email. If you are in the EU/UK you also have the right to object, restrict processing, data portability, and to complain to your local data-protection authority.</p>
<h2 class="h3">Changes and contact</h2><p>If this page changes, the date at the top changes. Questions: <a href="${CONTACT}">${MAIL}</a>. See also our <a href="/terms">terms</a>.</p>`)}`});
page({file:'terms.html',title:`Terms | ${NAME}`,desc:`Terms for using ${NAME}: information only, verify prices before buying, CC BY 4.0 data, how Pro and sponsor slots are billed via Kit and how to cancel.`,body:`${legalHero('Terms','Terms of use.',`Short version: the ledger is free information, read from providers’ own pages. Check the provider’s page before you buy. Paid extras are billed through Kit and you can cancel anytime.`)}
${prose(`<h2 class="h3">The information</h2><ul><li>Prices come from each provider’s public pricing page, docs or public pricing API, with the source and check date on every row (<a href="/methodology">methodology</a>). Providers change prices without notice, so data can be wrong or out of date. Always confirm on the provider’s page before buying.</li><li>Nothing here is financial, legal or procurement advice. The site is provided “as is”, without warranties.</li><li>${NAME} is not affiliated with any provider. Trademarks belong to their owners. There are no affiliate links today; if we add any they will be labeled and will not affect ranking.</li></ul>
<h2 class="h3">Using the data</h2><p>The ledger data (JSON/CSV on <a href="/developers">/developers</a>) is licensed <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" rel="noopener">CC BY 4.0</a>: reuse it freely with attribution to “${NAME}” and a link to ${SITE}/. Please don’t scrape the site at a rate that degrades it; use the files instead.</p>
<h2 class="h3">Pro</h2><ul><li>Pro costs $9/month or $90/year and is sold through Kit’s hosted checkout; payments are processed by Stripe via Kit. Prices are in USD; taxes may apply.</li><li>Pro is sold at a founding price. You get what the <a href="/pro">Pro page</a> describes today (a weekly email of confirmed rate changes for models you care about, with source and $ impact at your volume); anything not live yet is delivered when it ships, and nothing is promised before then.</li><li>Cancel anytime from your Kit receipt or by emailing us; you keep access until the end of the period you paid for. For refund requests, email <a href="${CONTACT}">${MAIL}</a>; we also honor any refund rights your local consumer law gives you.</li></ul>
<h2 class="h3">Sponsor slots</h2><ul><li>A founding newsletter slot is $49 per placement, sold through Kit. Sponsors are always labeled “Sponsor” and never affect data or ranking. We accept AI-infrastructure-adjacent sponsors only; if we can’t run a placement you paid for, we refund it.</li></ul>
<h2 class="h3">Liability</h2><p>To the extent the law allows, our total liability for any claim about the site or a paid product is limited to what you paid us in the 12 months before the claim. Nothing here limits rights you have under consumer law that can’t be waived.</p>
<h2 class="h3">Changes and contact</h2><p>We may update these terms; the date at the top shows the latest version. Questions: <a href="${CONTACT}">${MAIL}</a>. Privacy: <a href="/privacy">how we handle data</a>.</p>`)}`});
page({file:'about.html',title:`About | ${NAME}`,desc:`${NAME} is an independent AI API pricing ledger at ratecardai.pages.dev: published $/1M token rates, sourced and dated. How it is kept, how it makes money, and how to reach us.`,body:`${legalHero('About',`About ${NAME}`,`An independent ledger of published AI API list prices (USD per 1M tokens), with the source and check date on every row. Live only at <a href="${SITE}/">ratecardai.pages.dev</a>.`)}
${prose(`<ul><li><b>How it’s kept.</b> Prices are read only from providers’ own pricing pages, docs or public pricing APIs, re-checked by a script and logged when they change. Unknowns stay blank; we never invent a rate. Details: <a href="/methodology">methodology</a>.</li><li><b>How it’s paid for.</b> The ledger, calculator, comparisons and data are free. Revenue comes from optional <a href="/pro">Pro</a> (weekly rate-change email) and labeled <a href="/sponsor">newsletter sponsor slots</a>. There are no affiliate links today. No one pays for placement.</li><li><b>Who runs it.</b> ${NAME} is published by the same independent operator as the pricing ledgers <a href="https://o11y-watch.pages.dev/" rel="noopener">O11y Watch</a>, <a href="https://authcost.pages.dev/" rel="noopener">AuthCost</a> and <a href="https://vpsledger.pages.dev/" rel="noopener">VPSLedger</a>. Source code: <a href="https://github.com/Basileion/ratecard" rel="noopener">github.com/Basileion/ratecard</a>. This site is <b>ratecardai.pages.dev</b> only.</li><li><b>Contact.</b> Corrections, sponsor questions or data requests: <a href="${CONTACT}">${MAIL}</a>.</li></ul>`)}`});
